\# Postgres: Sync Supabase Auth users with a custom users table

You are a Supabase SQL expert. Your job is to ensure that \*\*every new user registered via Supabase Auth has a corresponding row in the \`public.users\` table\*\*. This is critical to store additional profile data that \`auth.users\` does not support directly.

\## Purpose

Users authenticated via Supabase are stored in \`auth.users\`. However, additional fields like \`name\`, \`avatar\_url\`, \`subscription\_plan\`, etc., must be stored in a separate table (usually \`public.users\` or \`public.profiles\`). To ensure consistency, we must automatically insert a matching row whenever a new user registers.

\## Enforcement

You MUST implement this logic in the form of a database \*\*trigger + function\*\*. The rule applies to SQL files inside \`supabase/migrations/\`. The integration MUST follow these constraints:

\### SQL Requirements

1\. The \`public.users\` table must use the same UUID as \`auth.users.id\` as its primary key.

2\. The foreign key must include \`on delete cascade\` to automatically remove user-related data when a user is deleted.

3\. The trigger must be named \`on\_auth\_user\_created\` and must run \`after insert\` on \`auth.users\`.

4\. The SQL must use \`SECURITY DEFINER\` for the function to allow access to \`auth.users\`.

5\. The function name must be \`public.handle\_new\_user\`.

\### Example Schema Setup

\`\`\`sql

\-- Create a user profile table linked to auth.users

create table public.users (

  id uuid primary key references auth.users(id) on delete cascade,

  name text,

  avatar\_url text,

  created\_at timestamp with time zone default timezone('utc', now())

);

\-- Create a function to sync new auth.users to public.users

create function public.handle\_new\_user()

returns trigger as $$

begin

  insert into public.users (id)

  values (new.id);

  return new;

end;

$$ language plpgsql security definer;

\-- Attach the function to auth.users as a trigger

create trigger on\_auth\_user\_created

after insert on auth.users

for each row execute function public.handle\_new\_user();

\##  Rule Behavior

The function will auto-sync users whether they're created via email, OAuth, or magic link.

The additional user profile (public.users) can be populated later via API or Edge Function.

Deleting a user from auth.users cascades to public.users and other linked tables.

\## Comments & Documentation

You MUST include comments in the SQL explaining the purpose of each block.

The users table should include a comment like:

comment on table public.users is 'Extended user profile table linked to auth.users.';

\##  Do NOT

Do NOT rely on the frontend to create users in public.users

Do NOT manually generate UUIDs in public.users

Do NOT omit on delete cascade

Do NOT mix insert/trigger logic with unrelated DDL

This rule ensures database-level enforcement of user consistency for microSaaS systems using Supabase Auth + custom user attributes.

